<title>USA: GS Industries KC steel plant hit by work stoppage.</title>
<headline>GS Industries KC steel plant hit by work stoppage.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLOTTE, N.C. 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>GS Industries Inc said Wednesday that negotiations for the labor contract between the United Steel Workers of America Local 13 and GST Steel Co, located in Kansas City, failed to produce a satisfactory resolution on all issues, leading to a work stoppage by the union at this facility.</p>
<p>The agreement that expired on March 31 had been extended for 24 hours in an effort to resolve the remaining open issues with the labor union, said the company.</p>
<p>The company said that it has made sizeable capital investments at GST Steel in the past few years and has yet to see the returns it had projected.</p>
<p>GS Industries is a producer of steel wire rod.</p>
</text>
